# AntTrajectoryAnalysis

A Python toolkit for extracting and analysing biological trajectories
from video recordings.

The software was developed for the quantitative analysis of ant
foraging trajectories and demonstrates the application of statistical
physics descriptors to biological motion.

Features:

- Automatic trajectory extraction using OpenCV
- Multi-object tracking
- Convex hull and explored area estimation
- Monte Carlo area calculation
- Occupancy maps
- Principal Component Analysis (PCA)
- Mean Squared Displacement (MSD)
- Straightness analysis
- Fractal dimension estimation
- Publication-quality figures

The software can also be adapted to other biological systems such as
protozoa, rotifers, nematodes, and other organisms exhibiting
approximately planar motion.

